learning from https://github.com/DoctorWkt/acwj
compile workflow: high-level input -> lexical analysis -> grammar analysis -> semantic analysis -> translate meaning -> low-level output

use #define extern_ extern to avoid repeated definitions
use global varible line, putBack and inFile

BNF: Backus-Naur Form
BNF description of grammar: sth: def1 | def2 | ...
definitions can be recursive
non-terminal symbols are symbols that are produced by rules
terminal symbols are symbols that are not produced by rules
recursive descent parsing
for example, math expressions
func expr()
	scan and check if the token is a digit, ERROR if not
	get next token
	if next token is EOF, return
	otherwise, call expr()

use Abstract Syntax Trees(ASTs) to store an expression for easier interpreting
in a mathmatical expression, the first node must be a digit
